From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: include: wine/sgnetctl.h in the makefile

Patch 0079 added include/wine/sgnetctl.h without listing it in
include/Makefile.in, so makedep could not find it when the Makefiles were
generated afresh (a clean build: "wine/sgnetctl.h: No such file or
directory ... could not create Makefile"). Incremental trees kept working,
which hid it.
---
--- a/include/Makefile.in
+++ b/include/Makefile.in
@@ -950,6 +950,7 @@
 	wine/schrpc.idl \
 	wine/server.h \
 	wine/server_protocol.h \
+	wine/sgnetctl.h \
 	wine/strmbase.h \
 	wine/svcctl.idl \
 	wine/test.h \
